Two-stage Miller op-amp (open-loop AC testbench)

* Supply and input
VDD vdd 0 dc 1.8
Vin inp 0 sine 0.9 100m 1k ac 1

* Bias: diode-connected reference + current source
Ibias vdd nb dc 20u
M8 nb nb 0 0 nmos W=10u L=1u

* First stage: tail source, NMOS input pair, PMOS mirror load
M5 nt nb 0 0 nmos W=20u L=1u
M1 n1 inm nt 0 nmos W=20u L=1u
M2 n2 inp nt 0 nmos W=20u L=1u
M3 n1 n1 vdd vdd pmos W=20u L=1u
M4 n2 n1 vdd vdd pmos W=20u L=1u

* Second stage: PMOS common-source + NMOS current sink
M6 out n2 vdd vdd pmos W=80u L=1u
M7 out nb 0 0 nmos W=40u L=1u

* Compensation and load
Cc n2 out 1p
CL out 0 2p

* DC feedback trick: sets the bias point at DC, opens the loop for AC
Lfb out inm 1G
Cfb inm 0 1G

.model nmos nmos (level=1 vto=0.5 kp=200u lambda=0.05 gamma=0.4 phi=0.7 tox=4n cgso=3e-10 cgdo=3e-10)
.model pmos pmos (level=1 vto=-0.5 kp=80u lambda=0.06 gamma=0.4 phi=0.7 tox=4n cgso=3e-10 cgdo=3e-10)

.op
.ac dec 20 1 1G
.noise v(out) Vin dec 20 1 1G
.end